      "content": "Your feelings and thoughts are being expressed with such sincerity and it's important to take them seriously. It's true that looking back can sometimes bring a sense of disconnection, especially when comparing your past accomplishments to your current efforts. Stepping away from creative endeavors can offer temporary relief, but it's also crucial to consider long-term happiness and fulfillment. Your current state doesn't diminish who you once were or who you can be in the future. There might be paths that can help you bridge the gap between your past and present selves. Many artists have found new ways to reconnect with their love for creation when they initially felt lost, and that could be a possibility for you as well. I encourage you to give your feelings some time to settle while also exploring everything, no matter how daunting it may seem right now. Self-care is paramount, and it's okay to decide what's best for your well-being at the moment. Remember, this isn't a graveyard of dreams; it's just a different kind of journey. If you'd like, I can help you brainstorm some strategies to cope during this challenging time or provide support in helping you make significant decisions. You're not alone in this.",
